__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
db.sqlite3
staticfiles/
.env
.vscode/

# Uploaded files: real CVs, payment proofs and voice notes.
# These were previously committed by accident — 28 real CVs (.pdf/.docx) are in
# the history under media/. Real people's home addresses, phone numbers and
# salary history do not belong in a git repository, and they stay there even
# after a later commit removes them.
#
# The files must be untracked AND purged from history, and the database rows
# that referenced them treated as compromised. Note that even after that, a CV
# published publicly is published: anyone who cloned the repo before the purge
# still has it, so anyone affected should be told.
media/
!.gitkeep

# .env.example IS committed; the real .env above never is.

# Throwaway debugging scratch. Rather than listing files one by one, ignore the
# whole shape: anything prefixed with `_` at the project root is a scratch
# harness, not part of the application. This is a deliberate exception to the
# normal "nothing is ignored" rule and it is why a set of orphaned diagnostic
# scripts, screenshots and query dumps could sit in the repo unexamined.
# The `tools/` directory holds the scripts that ARE meant to be kept.
/_*
/*.png
/*.log
/*.txt
!requirements.txt

# Local test databases. `db.sqlite3` is already listed above; this catches the
# ad-hoc ones that get created while running manage.py test.
/_*.sqlite3
/t.sqlite3
/test*.sqlite3
